{
  "scope": "Visible hardware configuration matrix, not automatic species tuning or a promoted default. Each class has explicit physical parameters; launch velocity is an observed output. Contact-settled reference snapshots and complete motor/load runs are both measured.",
  "protocol": "Same force-driven loading recipe as iteration4 at600Hz. Serialize one loaded state per setup, reconstruct that identical state for each300/600/1200Hz launch. Contact cache is reconstructed consistently; no encounter or control forces. Payload can eject over the rim before bead exit. First actual world impact after departure is observed from contact impulse; launch-branch hits fail usefulness.",
  "limitations": [
    "Readiness uses existing COM envelope; initial support contacts are reported separately. Reference snapshots additionally wait for observed contact with relative speed<0.35m/s sustained0.1s, at most3s. This is a measurement protocol, not forced settling or a gameplay timer.",
    "Net energy loss includes contacts and numerical residual, not a calibrated dissipation model. Step gains reveal position-correction/contact artifacts even when no net energy gain occurs.",
    "Stability shown for these snapshots only, not every loading history or hardware combination.",
    "Useful means positive horizontal and vertical velocity with at least~10m/s speed; it does not mean optimized range.",
    "Baseline ghost-cradle release remains unchanged; this channel remains optional."
  ],
